{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789314265,"nonce":"+XUYzuyWWjU9K1IpfqdmozYJfg8=","title":"The CI AOT lane lost its method devirtualization when --aot-profile was dropped on a Mac measurement","message":"bench_method_call: ash-aot 216ms on CI (126 on the NUC) against hybrid 171\n(104) and HL/C 158. Every other call bench is fastest in AOT.\n\na412823 removed `--aot-profile` from the CI AOT lane because, on a Mac,\nthe `cold` attribute on the fiber poll alone reached the profile's number\n(101.4 vs 101.2ms). It does not hold on Linux x86-64. From the CI\nartifacts, ash-aot method_call on EPYC 7763 runners: no profile, no cold\n222.6 / 227.0; profile only 134.8 / 129.9; profile + cold 97.6 / 97.8\n(0.63-0.66x hybrid); cold only, i.e. every sweep since a412823, 191-216\n(1.0-1.3x hybrid). The row lost about half its speed on Linux the hour the\nprofile was dropped, and the cold attribute by itself moved it ~0 on\nEPYC 9V74 (215.3/216.0 before, 215.4-216.3 after). Cost of the profile\nper the artifacts: aot_build_ms 1120 -\u003e 1495, off the bar by construction.\n\nThe hybrid LLVM body has no call in the loop: the receiver's type header\nis loaded once per iteration (`!invariant.load`), compared with Stepper's\n`hl_type*`, and the hit arm runs `mul 31 / srem 8 / add` inline; the\nvtable walk is on the miss arm only (`devirt method fast-arm 3`). The AOT\nbody does three dependent loads (obj-\u003et, t-\u003evobj_proto, vobj_proto[0]), a\nnull check and an indirect `blr` into a separate `@step` with its own\nframe, every iteration. The guard's type and target come from\n`callsite_profile`, which only the interpreter fills (`record_method`,\nash_interp ops.rs); AOT never interprets, so the JIT arm in\n`emit_air_call_method` (calls.rs ~853-870) finds nothing and the AOT arm\n(~960-977) fires only with `--pgo`, which CI omits on purpose. Even\n`--pgo` guards on the vtable SLOT after all three loads, because the\nprofile names a function, not a type. Nothing else differs: AIR has no\ndevirt pass, Cranelift emits the same indirect chain, and the AIR config\nis shared between promotion and AOT.\n\nTwo ways out. Restore `--aot-profile` in the lane (scripts/aot_bench.py\nstill has it) -- the like-for-like argument in bench.yml against HL/C is\nthe policy question. Or give the AOT arm a SPECULATIVE guard that needs no\nprofile: the static receiver type's own implementation as the candidate,\nguarded by `icmp eq ptr %type, @ash_type_N` on the receiver's header (the\nAOT type descriptor is a module global), direct call on hit, the vtable\npath on miss, so the inliner can take the hit arm. CHA cannot pick here:\nBenchMethodCall instantiates BOTH classes (`Sys.time() \u003c 0.0 ? new\nStepper2() : new Stepper()`, dead only at run time) and Stepper2 overrides\nstep; the earlier survey found 0 CHA-monomorphic CallMethod sites of 3883\nwith the std library linked. Whatever lands has to be measured on Linux;\nthe Mac never showed the gap.","files":null}]}